<li><strong>Target variable:</strong> <code>Appliances</code> â€” hourly appliance electricity consumption (Wh).</li>
<li><strong>Forecast horizon:</strong> 24 hours ahead (one full day), matching the assignment brief.</li>
<li><strong>Train/test split:</strong> For benchmark, ARMA, SARIMAX, and LSTM models, the <strong>last 24 hours</strong>
of the hourly series are held out as the test set; everything before that is training data.
This gives every model an identical, directly comparable forecast target.</li>
<li><strong>XGBoost test period:</strong> the feature-based model additionally uses the <strong>last 14 days</strong>
(336 hours) as a held-out test period (as specified in the brief) to evaluate performance
more robustly across many different daily contexts; the final 24 hours of that window is
also reported separately so it is directly comparable to the other models.</li>
<li><strong>Evaluation metrics:</strong> RMSE, MAE, and MAPE, computed on the held-out test window(s).</li>
</ul></span></div>
